  "question": {
    "text": "An electric dipole of mass m, charge q, and length \\(l\\) is placed in a uniform electric field \\(\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}}=\\mathrm{E}_0 \\hat{i}\\). When the dipole is rotated slightly from its equilibrium position and released, the time period of its oscillations will be:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "vk7Lg",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{1}{2 \\pi} \\sqrt{\\frac{m l}{2 q E_0}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "s8bRS",
      "text": "\\(2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{~m} l}{\\mathrm{qE}_0}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fu27h",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{1}{2 \\pi} \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\mathrm{~m} l}{\\mathrm{qE}_0}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "to6pp",
      "text": "\\(2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{~m} l}{2 \\mathrm{qE}_0}}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/o-rYU6u9TKO5l5DbQarB50wfBkW-UkCoGgUE11YviQ8.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$\\tau=P E_0 \\sin \\theta$\nIf $\\theta$ is small\n$\\begin{aligned}\n\\tau & =-\\left(P E_0\\right) \\theta \\\\\nI & =m\\left(\\frac{l}{2}\\right)^2 \\cdot 2=\\frac{m l^2}{2} \\\\\nT & =2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{m l^2}{2 \\cdot P E_0}}=2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{m l^2}{2 \\cdot q / E_0}} \\\\\nT & =2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{m l}{2 q E_0}}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
